# Gladiolus Amicitia (6/6): "When Gladiolus Amicitia enters, search your library for a land card, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle." and "Landfall - Whenever a land you control enters,
# another target creature you control gets +2/+2 and gains trample until end of turn." Turn 1 Bot1 casts a Memnite, then Gladiolus. The search takes a Mountain from its own library (not any land of
# Bot2's) tapped, and the Mountain entering is itself a landfall: the only other creature, Memnite, becomes 3/3 with trample (Gladiolus is not a legal target of "another"). Turn 3 an Island played
# gives it +2/+2 again, from a second trigger, and an Island Bot2 plays on turn 4 does nothing: "a land you control".

